---
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const docs = `${base}docs/`;
---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>Canon — always-on law</title>
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="Always-on law for AI agents. Git markdown. Never retrieved. Law, not memory."
    />
    <link rel="icon" href={`${base}canon-mark.png`} type="image/png" />
    <meta property="og:title" content="Canon" />
    <meta
      property="og:description"
      content="Always-on law for AI agents. Git markdown. Never retrieved."
    />
    <meta
      property="og:image"
      content="https://mattstyles333.github.io/canon/canon-og.png"
    />
    <style is:global>
      @import "../styles/canon.css";
    </style>
  </head>
  <body class="hero-page">
    <div class="hero-wrap">
      <nav class="hero-nav">
        <a class="mark" href={base}>Canon</a>
        <span>
          <a href={docs}>Docs</a>
          &nbsp;·&nbsp;
          <a href={`${docs}onboarding/`}>Onboarding</a>
          &nbsp;·&nbsp;
          <a href="https://github.com/mattstyles333/canon">GitHub</a>
        </span>
      </nav>

      <section class="hero-stage">
        <div>
          <p class="kicker">Law, not memory</p>
          <h1>Always-on.</h1>
          <p class="lede">
            Law for AI agents, stored as git markdown, never retrieved. Fork
            the repo. Replace <code>law/</code>. CI is the lock. MCP is an
            optional projection of git — not a brain.
          </p>
          <div class="cta-row">
            <a class="cta" href={`${docs}onboarding/`}>Onboarding</a>
            <a class="cta ghost" href={docs}>Read the docs</a>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="hero-visual">
          <img src={`${base}canon-hero.png`} alt="Canon" />
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="rules">
        <div>
          <h2>Not retrieval</h2>
          <p>
            Similarity search is not a constraint. Always-on law loads every
            session. If it is not in git, it is not policy.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h2>Fork, then replace</h2>
          <p>
            Northwind Coffee is a teaching example. Your organisation’s law
            lives in <code>law/</code>. Keep <code>AGENTS.md</code> under 80
            lines.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h2>CI is the lock</h2>
          <p>
            Agents rewrite policy if you let them. <code>check-law.sh</code>
            and GitHub Actions are the security layer. Not a prompt.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <p class="foot">MIT · v0.1.0 · Northwind is fictional</p>
    </div>
  </body>
</html>
